        "original_id": "4735170c-5cf8-5b1c-b8e0-72df62262a48",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Keebler Company\n- Products: Club Crackers, saltines, Cheez-It, Chips Deluxe, E.L. Fudge Cookies, Famous Amos, Fudge Shoppe Cookies, Murray cookies, Austin, Plantation, Vienna Fingers, Town House Crackers, Wheatables, Sandie's Shortbread, Chachos, Zesta Crackers\n- Topics: cracker design, baked snacks, brand marketing\n\nFacts:\n- The Keebler Company was founded in 1853.\n- The Keebler Company is the largest cookie and cracker manufacturer in the United States.\n- The Keebler Company has produced numerous baked snacks.\n- The Keebler Company has marketed brands including Cheez-It, Chips Deluxe, Club Crackers, E.L. Fudge Cookies, Famous Amos, Fudge Shoppe Cookies, Murray cookies, Austin, Plantation, Vienna Fingers, Town House Crackers, Wheatables, Sandie's Shortbread, Chachos, and Zesta Crackers.\n- Club Crackers are a brand of crackers made by the American Keebler Company.\n- Club Crackers resemble saltines, but Club Crackers are rectangular and have 18 holes in a 3x6 pattern.\n- Saltines have 13 holes in a 3-2-3-2-3 pattern.",
